  "review": {
    "entityID": "person:manasseh_1928",
    "book": "JOS",
    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "JOS 1:12 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Joshua spoke to the Reubenites, and to the Gadites, and to the half-tribe of Manasseh, saying,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 4:12 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The children of Reuben, and the children of Gad, and the half-tribe of Manasseh crossed over armed before the children of Israel, as Moses spoke to them."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 12:6 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Moses the servant of the LORD and the children of Israel struck them. Moses the servant of the LORD gave it for a possession to the Reubenites, and the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 13:7 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now therefore divide this land for an inheritance to the nine tribes and the half-tribe of Manasseh.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 13:29 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Moses gave an inheritance to the half-tribe of Manasseh. It was for the half-tribe of the children of Manasseh according to their families."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 13:31 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Half Gilead, Ashtaroth, and Edrei, the cities of the kingdom of Og in Bashan, were for the children of Machir the son of Manasseh, even for the half of the children of Machir according to their families."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 14:4 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "For the children of Joseph were two tribes, Manasseh and Ephraim. They gave no portion to the Levites in the land, except cities to dwell in, with their pasture lands for their livestock and for their property."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 16:4 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The children of Joseph, Manasseh and Ephraim, took their inheritance."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 16:9 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "together with the cities which were set apart for the children of Ephraim in the middle of the inheritance of the children of Manasseh, all the cities with their villages."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 17:1 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "This was the lot for the tribe of Manasseh, for he was the firstborn of Joseph. As for Machir the firstborn of Manasseh, the father of Gilead, because he was a man of war, therefore he had Gilead and Bashan."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 17:2 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "So this was for the rest of the children of Manasseh according to their families: for the children of Abiezer, for the children of Helek, for the children of Asriel, for the children of Shechem, for the children of Hepher, and for the children of Shemida. These were the male children of Manasseh the son of Joseph according to their families."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 17:3 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "But Zelophehad, the son of Hepher, the son of Gilead, the son of Machir, the son of Manasseh, had no sons, but daughters. These are the names of his daughters: Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 17:5 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Ten parts fell to Manasseh, in addition to the land of Gilead and Bashan, which is beyond the Jordan;"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 17:6 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "because the daughters of Manasseh had an inheritance among his sons. The land of Gilead belonged to the rest of the sons of Manasseh."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 17:7 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The border of Manasseh was from Asher to Michmethath, which is before Shechem. The border went along to the right hand, to the inhabitants of En Tappuah."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 17:8 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The land of Tappuah belonged to Manasseh; but Tappuah on the border of Manasseh belonged to the children of Ephraim."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 17:9 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The border went down to the brook of Kanah, southward of the brook. These cities belonged to Ephraim among the cities of Manasseh. The border of Manasseh was on the north side of the brook, and ended at the sea."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 17:10 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Southward it was Ephraim’s, and northward it was Manasseh’s, and the sea was his border. They reached to Asher on the north, and to Issachar on the east."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 17:11 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Manasseh had three heights in Issachar, in Asher Beth Shean and its towns, and Ibleam and its towns, and the inhabitants of Dor and its towns, and the inhabitants of Endor and its towns, and the inhabitants of Taanach and its towns, and the inhabitants of Megiddo and its towns."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 17:12 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Yet the children of Manasseh couldn’t drive out the inhabitants of those cities; but the Canaanites would dwell in that land."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 17:17 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Joshua spoke to the house of Joseph, that is, to Ephraim and to Manasseh, saying, “You are a numerous people, and have great power. You shall not have one lot only;"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 18:7 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "However, the Levites have no portion among you; for the priesthood of the LORD is their inheritance. Gad, Reuben, and the half-tribe of Manasseh have received their inheritance east of the Jordan, which Moses the servant of the LORD gave them.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 20:8 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Beyond the Jordan at Jericho eastward, they assigned Bezer in the wilderness in the plain out of the tribe of Reuben, Ramoth in Gilead out of the tribe of Gad, and Golan in Bashan out of the tribe of Manasseh."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 21:5 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The rest of the children of Kohath had ten cities by lot out of the families of the tribe of Ephraim, out of the tribe of Dan, and out of the half-tribe of Manasseh."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 21:6 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The children of Gershon had thirteen cities by lot out of the families of the tribe of Issachar, out of the tribe of Asher, out of the tribe of Naphtali, and out of the half-tribe of Manasseh in Bashan."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 21:25 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Out of the half-tribe of Manasseh, Taanach with its pasture lands, and Gath Rimmon with its pasture lands: two cities."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 21:27 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "They gave to the children of Gershon, of the families of the Levites, out of the half-tribe of Manasseh Golan in Bashan with its pasture lands, the city of refuge for the man slayer, and Be Eshterah with its pasture lands: two cities."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 22:1 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Joshua called the Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 22:7 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now to the one half-tribe of Manasseh Moses had given inheritance in Bashan; but Joshua gave to the other half among their brothers beyond the Jordan westward. Moreover when Joshua sent them away to their tents, he blessed them,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 22:9 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the half-tribe of Manasseh returned, and departed from the children of Israel out of Shiloh, which is in the land of Canaan, to go to the land of Gilead, to the land of their possession, which they owned, according to the commandment of the LORD by Moses."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 22:10 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "When they came to the region near the Jordan, that is in the land of Canaan, the children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the half-tribe of Manasseh built an altar there by the Jordan, a great altar to look at."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 22:11 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The children of Israel heard this, “Behold, the children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the half-tribe of Manasseh have built an altar along the border of the land of Canaan, in the region around the Jordan, on the side that belongs to the children of Israel.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 22:13 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The children of Israel sent to the children of Reuben, and to the children of Gad, and to the half-tribe of Manasseh, into the land of Gilead, Phinehas the son of Eleazar the priest."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 22:15 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "They came to the children of Reuben, and to the children of Gad, and to the half-tribe of Manasseh, to the land of Gilead, and they spoke with them, saying,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 22:21 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then the children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the half-tribe of Manasseh answered, and spoke to the heads of the thousands of Israel,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 22:30 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "When Phinehas the priest, and the princes of the congregation, even the heads of the thousands of Israel that were with him, heard the words that the children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the children of Manasseh spoke, it pleased them well."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 22:31 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Phinehas the son of Eleazar the priest said to the children of Reuben, to the children of Gad, and to the children of Manasseh, “Today we know that the LORD is among us, because you have not committed this trespass against the LORD. Now you have delivered the children of Israel out of the LORD’s hand.”"
      }
    ],
